infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Where exactly-once actually broke
  desc Four real incidents — none failed in the broker guarantee
  lists
    - label Stripe 2020 — consumer code
      desc Queue consumer dropped the Idempotency-Key on retry; customers charged twice. The broker delivered correctly; the consumer was not idempotent.
    - label AWS SQS 2019 — consumer-side race
      desc ChangeMessageVisibility raced an in-flight DeleteMessage, forcing redelivery. The visibility-timeout contract, not the broker, leaked the duplicate.
    - label Slack 2022 — zombie producer
      desc A rolling restart left producer sessions unfenced; Kafka EOS shipped duplicates for 6 minutes. Coordination state, not the delivery promise, failed.
    - label Stripe 2023 — operational procedure
      desc Unthrottled redrive of a 1M-message DLQ flooded the consumer pool and throttled the payment API. The runbook, not the broker, caused the outage.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #8b5cf6 #6366f1
